  "section_notes": "S1 is the strongest section, requiring 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, including suspected ones, with no wait for cause confirmation. S2 keeps an 8% maximum with no sales stop between 5% and 8%, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%, while exact per-model rates go to purchasers and regulators but are not published. S5 sets an 8/100k trigger that prompts notice and regulator assessment but makes recall discretionary, leaving the Ember 8 at 9.9 able to stay in the market through an open-ended corrective-action path, and S3's 72-month retrofit deadline also favours Northwind."
